  "agent_feedback": {
    "analysis": "The EKET table stores scheduling agreement schedule lines. It is used to manage the delivery of goods or services under a scheduling agreement. The table contains fields for the purchasing document number, item number, delivery schedule line counter, item delivery date, scheduled quantity, and other relevant information. The EKET table is typically used to create and manage scheduling agreements and to track the delivery of goods or services under those agreements. It is also used to generate purchase orders and other documents related to the procurement process.",
